# Per-worktree local config for the C28x dev harnesses.  --  TEMPLATE, committed.
#
# Copy this to `.c28x.env` (which is gitignored) at the root of a worktree and set
# the paths for THIS machine / THIS worktree. The harnesses under tests/ load it
# automatically via tests/_env.{sh,ps1}; `scripts/worktree.{sh,ps1} add` seeds one
# into every new worktree it creates. See docs/WORKTREES.md.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line. No quotes. Values may contain spaces and
# backslashes. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. A file set
# here WINS over an inherited shell environment variable of the same name.

# --- required: your Ghidra install root ---
# Used by run_disasm_test, run_fw_parity, and build_modifier. Give each worktree
# its OWN Ghidra install here if you want to run headless tests in two worktrees
# at once -- the module is a singleton within a single Ghidra install, so worktrees
# that share one install can only be tested one at a time (docs/WORKTREES.md).
GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=/opt/ghidra_12.1.2_PUBLIC
# Windows example (note: no quotes even with spaces):
# GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=C:\Users\you\Downloads\ghidra_12.1.2_PUBLIC_20260605\ghidra_12.1.2_PUBLIC

# --- optional: TI C2000 code-generation tools (run_fw_parity only) ---
# Root of a TI CGT install that contains bin/asm2000 and bin/dis2000.
# C2000WARE=/opt/ti/ti-cgt-c2000

# --- optional: JDK for build_modifier (else javac/jar are taken from PATH) ---
# JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/temurin-21-jdk
